@flexiarg operator/bare-continue-signal
@title Bare Continue Signal — "OK, Please Continue"
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-FzcUn1 turn-l7W2HH
@parent workshop/accountable-next-action-choice
@context An agent is mid-task in a supervised session and has just reported progress or paused; the operator holds the turn.

! conclusion: Record it as a trajectory-approval-and-handback: approve the current course unchanged and let the agent proceed; do not mine it for new requirements.

  + IF:
    The operator replies with a bare acknowledgement plus a continue directive ('OK, please continue'), supplying no new content, constraint, or amendment.

  + HOWEVER:
    The turn carries almost no information, yet it is still a deliberate operator act: it confirms the trajectory is acceptable and hands control back, and it is distinguishable both from silence and from 'OK, but…' amendments.

  + THEN:
    Record it as a trajectory-approval-and-handback: approve the current course unchanged and let the agent proceed; do not mine it for new requirements.

  + BECAUSE:
    It is the degenerate case of the operator pin: the operator exercises the next-action choice by reaffirming the incumbent action rather than selecting a new one — priority still flows from operator to agent, with zero re-ranking.
